              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_mtheory"} In M-theory
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+smooth+structure"} exotic smooth structure
            is called an
            = succeed "." do
              %em exotic 7-sphere
          %h2#Construction Milnor’s construction
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Milnor1956"} Milnor (1956)
            gave the first examples of exotic smooth structures on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+7-spheres"} exotic 7-spheres
            constructed in
            %a{:href => "#Milnor1956"} Milnor 1956
            are all examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibre+bundles"} fibre bundles
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibre"} fibre
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%284%29"} SO(4)
            (see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/8-manifold"} 8-manifold
            the section
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "8-manifold#ExoticBoundary7Spheres"} With exotic boundary 7-spheres
          %p
            By the classification of bundles on spheres via the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to SO(4)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_3(SO(4))
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "orthogonal+group#HomotopyGroups"} orthogonal group – Homotopy groups
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}\oplus\mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,m)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo ↠
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{m,n}\twoheadrightarrow S^4
            denote the real vector bundle corresponding to the integer pair
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m,n\in\mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{m,n}\cong E_{-m,-n}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#McEnroe15"} McEnroe 15, Lem. 6.14
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\in H^4(S^4)\cong\mathbb{Z}
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generator"} generator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+class"} Euler class
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+first+Pontryagin+class"} fractional first Pontryagin class
            are:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi α
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e(E_{m,n})
                  \=-(m+n)\alpha;
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi α
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{p_1(E_{m,n})}{2}
                  \=(n-m)\alpha.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#McEnroe15"}> McEnroe 15, Eq. (6.17) &amp; Eq. (6.29)
            )
          %p
            With the choice of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            on it, one has a disk bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↠
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(E_{m,n})\twoheadrightarrow S^4
            by taking the disks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^4\subset\mathbb{R}^4
            of each fiber, a sphere bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↠
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(E_{m,n})=\partial D(E_{m,n})\twoheadrightarrow S^4
            by taking the spheres
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3\subset\mathbb{R}^4
            of each fiber as well as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(E_{m,n})=D(E_{m,n})/S(E_{m,n})
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
          %p
            A special case is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi ℍ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo ↠
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi q
                    %mo :
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_\mathbb{H}\colon\mathbb{H}^2\supset S^7\twoheadrightarrow S^4\cong\mathbb{H}P^1,[q,p]\mapsto[q:p]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+SU%282%29-bundle"} principal SU(2)-bundle
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+bundle"} sphere bundle
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundle"} real vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi γ
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mo ↠
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\gamma_\mathbb{H}^{1,1})_\mathbb{R}\twoheadrightarrow S^4
            represented by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℍ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℍ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi B
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi B
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^4
                  \\cong\mathbb{H}P^1
                  \\hookrightarrow\mathbb{H}P^\infty
                  \\cong B SU(2)
                  \\hookrightarrow B SO(4),
          %p
            which corresponds to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m=0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#McEnroe15"} McEnroe 15, p. 11
          %p
            More generally for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+m=1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morse+function"} Morse function
            with exactly two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+points"} critical points
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(E_{m,n})
            exists, implying that it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            according to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reeb+sphere+theorem"} Reeb sphere theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphic"} diffeomorphic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(E_{m,n})
            and the disk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^8
            together along their common boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(E_{m,n})\cong S^7
            using a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            to obtain the closed
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/8-manifold"} 8-manifold
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 7
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 8
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M_{m,n}
                  \=D(E_{m,n})+_{S^7}D^8.
          %p
            Due to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^4(M_{m,n},\mathbb{Z})\cong\mathbb{Z}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^8(M_{m,n},\mathbb{Z})\cong\mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection+form"} intersection form
            is described by a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            and hence the signature can only be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(M_{m,n})=1
            with suitable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirzebruch%27s+signature+theorem"} Hirzebruch's signature theorem
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 45
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mn 7
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %msubsup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma(M_{m,n})
                  \=\frac{1}{45}\langle 7p_2(M_{m,n})-p_1^2(M_{m,n}),[M_{m,n}]\rangle
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#McEnroe15"}> McEnroe 15, Thrm. 6.37
            )
          %p
            Since the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+class"} Pontrjagin class
            is known, but the second
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+class"} Pontrjagin class
            is not,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"} John Milnor
            eliminated it by projecting to the following
            = succeed "-7" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modulo"} modulo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi m
                          %mo −
                          %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn 2
                          %mi mod
                          %mn 7
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msubsup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mi mod
                          %mn 7
                          %mo =
                          %mn 45
                          %mi σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi mod
                          %mn 7
                          %mo =
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 45
                          %mi mod
                          %mn 7
                          %mo =
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇒
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi E
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi m
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mi n
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mn 2
                              %mo )
                            %mn 2
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi m
                          %mo −
                          %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn 2
                          %mi mod
                          %mn 7
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  4(m-n)^2 mod 7
                  \=-\langle p_1^2(M_{m,n}),[M_{m,n}]\rangle mod 7
                  \=45\sigma(M_{m,n}) mod 7
                  \=\pm 45 mod 7
                  \=\pm 3 \\
                  \\Rightarrow
                  \\left(\frac{p_1(E_{m,n})}{2}\right)^2
                  \=(m-n)^2 mod 7
                  \=1.
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#McEnroe15"}> McEnroe 15, Thrm. 6.44
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(E_{m,n})
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m+n=1
            is then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphic"} diffeomorphic
            to the standard
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 7
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            if and only if this equation holds and hence the
            = succeed "-7" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modulo"} modulo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo −
                  %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mi mod
                  %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m-n)^2-1 mod 7
            vanishes. Examples like
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m=1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
            show, that this doesn’t have to be true. In this case, the contradiction in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirzebruch%27s+signature+theorem"} Hirzebruch's signature theorem
            is resolved by the previously used assumption of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(E_{m,n})
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphic"} diffeomorphic
            to obtain the glueing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{m,n}
            to not be true.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{m,n}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m+n=1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo −
                  %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mi mod
                  %mn 7
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m-n)^2 mod 7\neq 1
            is then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
            but not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphic"} diffeomorphic
            to the standard
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 7
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
          %p
            By using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+sum"} connected sum
            operation, the set of smooth, non-diffeomorphic structures on the
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 28
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/{28}
            and
            %a{:href => "#Brieskorn66"} Brieskorn (1966)
            found the generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo #
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo #
                        %mi Σ
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mn 28
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underbrace{\Sigma\#\cdots\#\Sigma}_28
            is the standard sphere.
          %p
            Review includes (
            %a{:href => "#Kreck10"}> Kreck 10, chapter 19
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#McEnroe15"} McEnroe 15
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#JoachimWraith"} Joachim-Wraith
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromoll-Meyer+sphere"} Gromoll-Meyer sphere
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsNearHorizonGeometriesOfBlackM2Branes As near-horizon geometries of black M2-branes
          %p
            From the point of view of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/8-manifolds"} 8-manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with (exotic)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundaries"} boundaries
            in
            %a{:href => "#Construction"} Milnor’s construction
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+limits"} near horizon limits
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2+brane"} M2 brane
            spacetimes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
